  "worked_solution": "When we divide the two functions, we get a constant, and the limit of a constant is just the constant itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{9{x}^{6}}{(-4{x}^{6})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }(-\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
